what_i_learned: |
  Today our team continued building the foundation for our research project. We spent time reviewing research papers to better understand the current work being done in our field and to identify ideas that could strengthen our own project. Reading the literature helped me see how researchers support their work with evidence and explain the reasoning behind their methods.

  We also continued making progress on our design document by refining different sections and discussing how to clearly communicate our project's goals. Working through the document helped me better understand how important planning is before beginning implementation.

  Throughout the day, our team collaborated to share ideas, ask questions, and provide feedback on one another's work. These discussions helped us gain a better understanding of our project and ensured that everyone was moving in the same direction.

  Overall, today reinforced the importance of preparation and teamwork. Every discussion and revision brought us one step closer to beginning the implementation phase of our research.

blockers: |
  One challenge today was deciding how to organize the information we gathered from several research papers into a clear and focused direction for our project. It took careful discussion to determine which ideas were the most relevant to our goals.

reflection: |
  Today reminded me that research is built on a strong foundation of planning and continuous learning. Although we were not writing code, the work we completed was just as important because it will guide the decisions we make throughout the rest of the project.

  I enjoyed collaborating with my teammates and hearing different perspectives during our discussions. Everyone brought unique ideas to the table, which helped strengthen both our design document and our understanding of the research.

  Overall, today was another productive step toward building a successful research project, and I feel more confident about the direction our team is taking.
